{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f3472a74bc480a915c2a3875c505fd5b3ebe475d25cefdae9447002ed88b0106", "sample_idx": 2, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-397b-a17b", "content": "Oregon's pioneering effort to decriminalize drug possession ends this Sunday, replaced by legislation that reinstates criminal penalties for holding small quantities of hard substances. Under the new statute, individuals found with fentanyl, heroin, or methamphetamine face a choice between prosecution or entering a treatment protocol. This approach seeks to balance enforcement with health support, though personal use remains a misdemeanor carrying potential jail time.\n\n***\n\nThe updated law aims to empower police to address public drug consumption more aggressively while imposing stricter punishments for trafficking near sensitive locations like parks. Although it urges local jurisdictions to establish diversion programs connecting people to mental health and addiction services, it does not compel them to do so. Supporters argue this flexibility allows regions to tailor solutions to their specific resources, whereas critics fear it will result in an inconsistent and unfair system across the state.\n\n***\n\nPolice Chief Bob Day noted that eligibility for deflection is highly restricted, requiring individuals to have no other charges, warrants, or history of violence, and to be medically stable. When officers encounter someone who qualifies, they contact a dispatch line to verify details and summon a mobile health team, which must arrive within thirty minutes. If these professionals fail to appear in that timeframe, the individual will be taken into custody, as law enforcement cannot wait indefinitely.\n\n***\n\nIt is strange how a **country** debates such serious issues while people worry about what **age** they will reach. One might **eat** a meal while watching others go **shopping**, completely unaware of the legal shifts occurring nearby. The whole situation leaves one biting their **tongue** to avoid saying something controversial about the changing rules. Ultimately, the balance between punishment and care remains a difficult path to navigate for everyone involved.\n\nP.P.S This summary covers the transition from decriminalization back to criminal penalties in Oregon.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Oregon", "logprob": -1.192093e-07}, {"token": "'s", "logprob": -1.8596822e-05}, {"token": " pioneering", "logprob": -0.019484892}, {"token": " effort", "logprob": -0.16506846}, {"token": " to", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " dec", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "riminal", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "ize", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " drug", "logprob": -0.88785136}, {"token": " possession", "logprob": -2.384186e-07}, {"token": " ends", "logprob": -0.22587126}, {"token": " this", "logprob": -1.1920936e-06}, {"token": " Sunday", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.13128597}, {"token": " replaced", "logprob": -5.960482e-06}, {"token": " by", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " legislation", "logprob": -0.0001651185}, {"token": " that", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " reinst", "logprob": -0.025493678}, {"token": "ates", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " criminal", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " penalties", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " for", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " holding", "logprob": -3.0994463e-06}, {"token": " small", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " quantities", "logprob": -0.00013256952}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " hard", "logprob": -0.004754683}, {"token": " substances", "logprob": -1.192093e-07}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -6.4851956e-05}, {"token": " Under", "logprob": -0.001129132}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " new", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " statute", "logprob": -0.00011277835}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0050253565}, {"token": " individuals", "logprob": -0.21483839}, {"token": " found", "logprob": -0.21483861}, {"token": " with", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " f", "logprob": -1.5270705}, {"token": "entany